Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// This strategy generates ordinary explanatory text freely when outside a
// constrained arithmetic span, but it opportunistically opens a span when the
// "<<"" token is competitive with the current argmax. The key repair from the
// previous version is that we never enter constrained mode merely because an
// arbitrary sampled token happened to equal or contain "<<"; instead, the only
// transitions from unconstrained to constrained are via OpenConstrainedSpan or
// by explicitly appending the literal token "<<". That makes the suffix story
// simple: whenever insideConstrainedOut becomes true, currentConstrainedOut is
// reset to [] immediately after appending only the opening delimiter, so the
// active constrained contents are always exactly the suffix after the delimiter.
//
// Inside a constrained span, the strategy first checks whether the current
// constrained contents already form a complete parser prefix; only then may it
// call CloseConstrainedSpan. Otherwise it speculates with the current argmax:
// if the argmax is parser-valid and not EOS, it samples once from the same
// logits, appends the sampled token if that sampled token is also parser-valid,
// and otherwise falls back to appending the parser-valid argmax. If the argmax
// itself is not parser-valid, it uses ConstrainedStep to obtain a valid next
// token. EOS is always terminal and causes an immediate break.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
// - Unconstrained/no-open branch: we stay outside constrained mode, so
//   insideConstrainedOut is false and the implication is vacuous.
// - Unconstrained/open branch: OpenConstrainedSpan appends only the opening
//   delimiter and returns insideConstrainedOut = true with
//   currentConstrainedOut = []; parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition.
// - Constrained/close branch: we call CloseConstrainedSpan only under
//   parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut); afterward we are outside, so
//   the implication is vacuous.
// - Constrained/speculative-append branches: AppendConstrainedToken is called
//   only with a token proved valid by IsTokenValidNext, either the sampled token
//   or the argmax, so validity of the new constrained prefix is preserved.
// - Constrained/fallback branch: ConstrainedStep returns a parser-valid next
//   token or EOS; on EOS we break before changing state, otherwise
//   AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity.
//
// suffix:
// - Unconstrained/no-open branch: we remain outside constrained mode, so the
//   suffix implication is vacuous.
// - Unconstrained/open branch: OpenConstrainedSpan appends only "<<"" and sets
//   currentConstrainedOut := []; since the tracked constrained contents have
//   length 0, generated[|generated|..] == [] holds immediately.
// - Constrained/close branch: CloseConstrainedSpan appends ">>" and resets to
//   outside mode, so the implication is vacuous afterward.
// - Constrained/speculative-append branches: AppendConstrainedToken appends the
//   same token to both generated and currentConstrainedOut, so if the old
//   currentConstrainedOut matched the suffix before the append, the new one
//   matches the suffix after the append.
// - Constrained/fallback branch: identical reasoning to the speculative append;
//   if EOS is returned we break without changing generated or the tracked suffix.
//
// cost:
// - Unconstrained/no-open and unconstrained/open branches both use one raw
//   ChooseNextTokenUnconstrained call, then manually bump helpers.cost by 1, and
//   also increment steps once.
// - Constrained/close branch uses CloseConstrainedSpan, which bumps cost by 1
//   internally, and we increment steps once.
// - Constrained/speculative branches use one raw sample with one manual cost
//   bump, and AppendConstrainedToken itself does not bump cost; again steps is
//   incremented once.
// - Constrained/fallback branch uses ConstrainedStep, which bumps cost by 1
//   internally, and we increment steps once; if EOS is returned, the break
//   happens after that single accounted step.
//
// progress:
// - In the unconstrained branches, either we append one ordinary token or we use
//   OpenConstrainedSpan to append exactly one delimiter token; then steps grows
//   by 1.
// - In the constrained/close branch, CloseConstrainedSpan appends exactly one
//   token ">>" and steps grows by 1.
// - In the constrained/speculative and constrained/fallback append branches,
//   AppendConstrainedToken appends exactly one token and steps grows by 1.
// - In any EOS branch, we break after incrementing steps for the sampling action
//   but without appending, so |generated| still satisfies the bound.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;
helpers.cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

